#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046660} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433116} :activity/id #uuid "0bc8f6b6-23d6-5738-be30-08a0c3cfbf5e" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048997 :topic/id #uuid "d20a7fc8-1ce1-5256-b63f-ebdb4499588c" :topic/math-academy-id 2053} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433114 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433111 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d76d167-e492-51ee-9cfd-8d82c4f98110" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433096} {:answer/id #uuid "73bbbd95-9078-522a-a479-9f6cd50aa8e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433097} {:answer/id #uuid "75ef54fd-3fd5-53a2-9cc3-b6d5ef0e7696" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433099} {:answer/id #uuid "89078605-cf1e-5560-98b3-4b7333c47f0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433101} {:answer/id #uuid "8f882acc-8e4c-55d3-b6d7-84fb97565dbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{20}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433103}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433103} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2bfe536-1acc-532a-b70b-2b468372d22d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433109}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6188e65a-2be8-551f-95a7-3b11de49478d" :question/math-academy-id "q-163119" :question/problem "Find the volume of the solid region enclosed by the plane $x=-2,$ the surface $x={z}^{2}+y,$ and the planes $y=0,$ $y=2,$ $z=0,$ $z=1.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our solid can be written as a type II region: \n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1,\\,\\,-2\\le x\\le {z}^{2}+y\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-2}^{{z}^{2}+y}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[x]_{x=-2}^{x={z}^{2}+y}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{z}^{2}+y-(-2)\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{z}^{2}+y+2\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{3}{z}^{3}+(y+2)z]}_{z=0}^{z=1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{3}+y+2\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{7}{3}+y\\,dy \\\\  & ={[\\frac{7}{3}y+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}\\cdot 2+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {2}^{2}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "15cb8356-aeba-5ea0-a7ab-4e524fdb6298"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433115 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433113 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5239f75a-0829-5cc8-a34d-c4a20eabec56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433094} {:answer/id #uuid "87567b3e-7270-57b1-acc7-cab013de2d09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433100} {:answer/id #uuid "8d0c5b03-77db-5e64-8a51-12b2e2349e9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433102} {:answer/id #uuid "9c1e2b57-9bf1-517e-ac51-8b35d51e8bb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433104} {:answer/id #uuid "ffc1ff97-663c-52fc-b66c-d6dbd7166ad9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433107}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433100} :answer-field/id #uuid "678a936d-2d59-5cda-bb5b-7ba53ed50f15" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433108}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "8fb4dc8a-610a-5632-95eb-19ebf2c9f8b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-161697" :question/problem "![](images/a0/a0ad9cb5ea68b0018680d57d86d88a8dfcf7581a238e9368f566b2396f119579.png)\n\nFind the volume of the solid region above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the right one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" :question/worked-solution "![](images/d7/d72b3c8aac80a46894d2b7c0c4956ced9eb5b4ebd663b73ba86096550e993bb8.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type III region\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3+\\frac{x}{3}-z\\},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2\\}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](images/a2/a2dbcefff1b7c28156f117b012c522dd65bca1c1ddd9e2bac4bf2e6ea1ce3722.png)\n\nHence, the type III representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3+\\frac{x}{3}-z\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3+x/3-z}dy\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[y]_{y=0}^{y=3+x/3-z}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(3+\\frac{x}{3}-z)-0\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}3+\\frac{x}{3}-z\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{[(3+\\frac{x}{3})z-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}((3+\\frac{x}{3})(2)-\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2})-0\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}4+\\frac{2x}{3}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[4x+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=3} \\\\  & =(12+3)-0 \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "3af6cb17-64ea-5a89-8d5c-b4cd183ea4db" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433118}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433116 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129762 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85287494-343a-5f08-8ce3-ddb465ec63b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128054} {:answer/id #uuid "95b618bf-4be2-55d9-bc12-c665f2e6b2d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128055} {:answer/id #uuid "9b237bdf-4e5a-52ce-8767-7d03eb67eccd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128056} {:answer/id #uuid "ec24a157-5b5e-5058-9e5e-049671ca1051" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{33}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128057} {:answer/id #uuid "49464d90-4a8f-5d53-9d01-28c5d5654e10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128058}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128058} :answer-field/id #uuid "1adf921f-3910-55f5-9228-74e4653b36b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128053}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "58e657fe-ad6a-53ef-9cfa-164db29f5116" :question/math-academy-id "q-40312" :question/problem "![](images/c2/c24eb387b430ae40e7c5ec0747eb8570df21ebbe4535fd1305676219ad5c83f1.png)\n\nFind the volume of the solid region above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the front one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" :question/worked-solution "![](images/d0/d00feacd712c1ca185a8975e8b6343f9937f254631614242003f1d76c1427ffe.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type II region\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 2+y-z\\},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD=\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2\\}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](images/59/59b7304dcc07ac38c093b7d8d29d4b4079f192cd9fd0385db9f1981e4640eceb.png)\n\nHence, the type II representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 2+y-z\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2+y-z}dx\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[x]_{x=0}^{x=2+y-z}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(2+y-z)-0\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2+y-z\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{[(2+y)z-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}((2+y)(2)-\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2})-0\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}2+2y\\,dy \\\\  & =[2y+{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=3} \\\\  & =(2(3)+{3}^{2})-0 \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "808ca638-ac49-5675-8a17-db421c44f255" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433117}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433117 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129763 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ef77ed18-249f-537b-8615-5306a3284672" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128061} {:answer/id #uuid "4062cf11-2488-5c94-8710-b203cad7b0c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128063} {:answer/id #uuid "5d0de3e4-c134-5ea7-b5dc-a5a628bbec37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128064} {:answer/id #uuid "4e0627ca-90a4-5c2d-835c-b255053c8381" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433093} {:answer/id #uuid "e249f9ca-86be-5b5a-b69e-663670da563c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433105}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128063} :answer-field/id #uuid "25782da8-dd94-5fd2-acba-47173bb4f81d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128059}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "77433c48-7de7-5d10-a89d-7533049beb31" :question/math-academy-id "q-40317" :question/problem "Find the volume of the solid $R$ given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\pi ,\\,-2\\le y\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type I region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{-2}^{2}[z]_{z=0}^{z=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-0\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡x[y]_{y=-2}^{y=2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,(2-(-2))\\,dx \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,dx \\\\  & =-4[\\operatorname{cos}⁡x]_{x=0}^{x=\\pi } \\\\  & =-4(-1-1) \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "c83aa896-3d0a-5926-8f0d-13b4a640fdef" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433115}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433118 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433112 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3740f966-0f93-528e-8cf0-ad5178dfa0c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9-6{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433091} {:answer/id #uuid "4dbf4c0b-b5df-5421-9edb-f86c8c2c705e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6-6{y}^{2}-2{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433092} {:answer/id #uuid "53329c60-d1ff-54b3-961f-07a95f0e51c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3+3{y}^{2}-2{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433095} {:answer/id #uuid "75a7954b-84e1-59d9-a8f5-f24af99eff69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6+9{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433098} {:answer/id #uuid "e57d5e52-da19-5261-a231-8c6edbb04f78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3-3{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433106}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433092} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0c34a23-22e6-559b-8ba1-968780133734" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433110}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "6fae9a19-909c-5d4f-9c8f-4d34e1cb3eba" :question/math-academy-id "q-161713" :question/problem "Consider the solid enclosed between the paraboloid $x={y}^{2}+2{z}^{2}$ and the parabolic cylinder $x=3-2{y}^{2},$ whose volume can be written in terms of double integrals, as follows:\n\n$$\nV={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{a(y)}^{b(y)}\\,f(y,z)\\,dz\\,dy\n$$\n\nWhat is ${a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to determine the projection of the intersection of our surfaces onto the $yz$-plane. So, let's find where they intersect.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2} & =3-2{y}^{2} \\\\ 3{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2} & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the projection of the intersection in the $yz$-plane is an ellipse.\n\nNotice that our solid can be written as a type II region: \n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2}\\le x\\le 3-2{y}^{2}\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the interior of the ellipse $3{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2}=3.$ \n\nAs a result, the volume of $R$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2}}^{3-2{y}^{2}}\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(3-2{y}^{2})-({y}^{2}+2{z}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}3-3{y}^{2}-2{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the boundary of $D$ consists of \n\n- the lower part $z=-\\sqrt{\\frac{3(1-{y}^{2})}{2}},$ and\n\n- the upper part $z=\\sqrt{\\frac{3(1-{y}^{2})}{2}},$\n\nfor $-1\\le y\\le 1.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}3-3{y}^{2}-2{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3(1-{y}^{2})/2}}^{\\sqrt{3(1-{y}^{2})/2}}\\,3-3{y}^{2}-2{z}^{2}\\,dz\\,dy.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f & ={(-\\sqrt{\\frac{3(1-{y}^{2})}{2}})}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{\\frac{3(1-{y}^{2})}{2}})}^{2}+(3-3{y}^{2}-2{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3(1-{y}^{2})}{2}+\\frac{3(1-{y}^{2})}{2}+(3-3{y}^{2}-2{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =6-6{y}^{2}-2{z}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "fe1c9984-4492-5bc7-9f8a-f367a564a7b2" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433114}}] :activity/title "Calculating Volumes of Solids Using Triple Integrals" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433090}]}
